course: dictionary
lesson: 11173
title: Wingless creatures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wingless is a word with two parts: wing and -less. The ending -less means without, so wingless means without wings. Test it by putting "without wings" into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
explain: «Head lice are tiny wingless insects that live only on people's heads.» The clue is in the next part of the sentence: head lice cannot jump or fly, they only crawl from hair to hair. So wingless tells you that they have no wings.
explain: «The glow-worm is a beetle: the wingless female makes a cold green light in her tail.» The female has no wings, but the flying males can still find her by her light. Wingless describes what a creature has, or does not have, and it is a clue about how it moves.
explain: Wingless means no wings at all. A bird with tiny wings that cannot be used is not the same as a wingless creature, so read the whole sentence to find out which one the author means.
fact: Wingless means having no wings.
fact: The ending -less means without, so hopeless means without hope.
fact: «Fleas» are tiny wingless insects with six legs, and their long back legs help them jump.
fact: «Silverfish» are wingless insects with three long tails.
fact: Wingless insects cannot fly, so they get around by crawling, jumping or running.
exercise: «Head lice are tiny wingless insects that live only on people's heads.» What does wingless mean here? | Having very big wings | Having wings that are wet | Having wings that glow | *Having no wings
exercise: «Fleas are tiny wingless insects with six legs.» How many legs do fleas have? | Ten | Eight | Four | *Six
exercise: «Silverfish are wingless insects with three long tails.» Find and copy the word that means without wings. | *wingless | insects | silverfish | tails
test: «The glow-worm is a beetle: the wingless female makes a cold green light.» What does wingless tell us about the female? | She has long, bright wings | She is very fast | She is a bird | *She has no wings
test: «Head lice cannot jump or fly, only crawl from hair to hair.» Which word tells you that head lice have no wings? | Tiny | People's | *Wingless | Insects
exam: «Silverfish» are wingless insects, so what does wingless mean? | Having wings that are very long | Having wings only in the summer | *Having no wings at all | Having tiny wings that cannot be used
